course: dictionary
lesson: 11983
title: Words that prove something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A certification is official proof. It shows that someone has passed a test, or that something meets a set standard. Look for clue words such as test, passed, trained or standard. «Mia got her swimming certification after passing the pool test.» The clues passed and test tell you that certification means official proof that Mia can swim safely.
explain: Certification can also mean the document or award that shows the proof. «The electrician showed us her certification before she started work.» Here the certificate is the paper, and certification is the official approval behind it. Lifeguards, first-aiders and electricians often need certification so that people can trust their skills.
explain: In films and games, certification means the age rating. «The film has a 12A certification, so younger children need an adult with them.» The clue is the word film. A sentence about a test points to one meaning, and a sentence about a film or game points to another. Always check the words around the word.
fact: Certification means official proof that someone or something has met a standard.
fact: «Certification» can also mean the official document or award that shows this proof.
fact: For films and games, certification is the age rating, such as U, PG, 12A, 15 or 18 in the UK.
fact: In the USA, film ratings include G, PG, PG-13 and R.
fact: Lifeguards, electricians and first-aiders often need certification before they can work.
exercise: «Ravi got his first-aid certification at the school course.» What does certification mean here? | A holiday in the sun | A pair of new trainers | * An official proof that he has passed a test | A loud argument with a teacher
exercise: «The film has a 15 certification.» What does certification mean in this sentence? | The name of the director | * The age rating for the film | A rough, scary sound | A map of the cinema
exercise: Which of these jobs often needs certification before a person can work? | * An electrician | A puddle | A sandcastle builder | A kite flyer
test: «Her swimming certification was printed on a gold card.» What does certification mean in this sentence? | A feeling of being cold | * An official award that shows she passed | A shop that sells cards | A kind of swimming stroke
test: «The game's certification was shown on the box.» What does certification mean here? | Its best player | * Its age rating | Its price in the shops | Its story ending
exam: Which sentence uses certification to mean an age rating? | * «The film's certification is 12A.» | «The lifeguard showed her certification.» | «Our school gave us a music certification.» | «The electrician needs safety certification.»
